# Cursor Rule — Coding

Follow `.ai/04-coding.md`.

- Clear, intention-revealing names.
- Strict type safety; avoid `any` unless justified.
- Handle errors at the right boundary; never swallow silently.
- Never log secrets, tokens, PII.
- Comments explain WHY, not WHAT; no dead commented code.
- Check the project already uses a library before adding it; prefer deps ≥ 7 days old; avoid floating ranges.
- Use env vars for environment-specific values; never hardcode secrets.
- Reuse before create; avoid premature abstraction.
- Prefer boring, understandable code over clever code.
